#
# Conformance case: profiles/goal-rdf-list-functions (#1009 §5)
# AC: the reasoning layer backs the first-class RDF list functions
# (gmeow:listLength/listContains/…) by walking the rdf:first/rdf:rest chain — the
# backward-goal Prolog analog of the forward-chase `rl:list-member` recursion. A
# membership goal over the list (x y z) returns {x, y, z}; a length goal returns 3.
#
# No forward rules: the list EDB lives in input.nq; the list operations are the
# backward goals in queries/.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/profiles/goal-rdf-list-functions/> .

# Schema: the element sort used by the projection back-ends.
ex:Element a logic:Kind .
